1928
02:37:12,047 --> 02:37:19,237
identical. When using two-dimensional arrays and lists, the advantages of arrays are

1929
02:37:19,237 --> 02:37:26,426
clear. To return the second item of the first row in our two-dimensional object, the

1930
02:37:26,426 --> 02:37:27,710
array syntax is

1931
02:37:27,710 --> 02:37:34,153
one square bracket. The analogous list syntax is a bit more verbose as you have to

1932
02:37:34,153 --> 02:37:40,675
surround both the zero and the one with square brackets. To return the first column

1933
02:37:40,675 --> 02:37:47,197
of values in our 2D object, the array syntax is square bracket, colon, comma, zero,

