1939
02:38:12,622 --> 02:38:18,378
simple as enclosing this inequality in square brackets. To do this using a list, we

1940
02:38:18,378 --> 02:38:24,133
need to write a for loop to filter the list, or use a list comprehension. In either

1941
02:38:24,133 --> 02:38:24,480
case,

1942
02:38:24,480 --> 02:38:29,505
using a NumPy array to index is less verbose and has a faster runtime. Now that

1943
02:38:29,505 --> 02:38:34,657
we've covered powerful and efficient NumPy arrays, let's start putting what we've

1944
02:38:34,657 --> 02:38:40,000
learned into practice. In this lesson, we'll learn how to examine the runtime of our

1945
02:38:40,000 --> 02:38:45,499
code. As mentioned in the previous chapter, runtime is an important consideration

1946
02:38:45,499 --> 02:38:50,795
when thinking about efficiency. Comparing runtimes between two code bases that

1947
02:38:50,795 --> 02:38:55,751
