03:42:58,456 --> 03:43:02,660
to learn about decorators, a powerful way of modifying the behavior of functions.

2726
03:43:02,660 --> 03:43:06,969
But first, we need to build up some foundational concepts that will make decorators

2727
03:43:06,969 --> 03:43:11,225
easier to understand. The main thing you should take away from this lesson is that

2728
03:43:11,225 --> 03:43:15,273
functions are just like any other object in Python. They are not fundamentally

2729
03:43:15,273 --> 03:43:17,090
different from lists, dictionaries,

2730
03:43:17,090 --> 03:43:22,039
data frames, strings, integers, floats, modules, or anything else in Python. And

2731
03:43:22,039 --> 03:43:27,050
because functions are just another type of object, you can do anything to or with

2732
03:43:27,050 --> 03:43:32,060
them that you would do with any other kind of object. You can take a function and

2733
03:43:32,060 --> 03:43:37,257
assign it to a variable, like x. Then, if you wanted to, you could call x instead of

