3132
04:12:05,300 --> 04:12:10,534
During this course, we are going to write a complete unit test suit for this example

3133
04:12:10,534 --> 04:12:15,456
project. It's going to be fun and exciting. This will prepare you to write unit

3134
04:12:15,456 --> 04:12:20,565
tests for your own projects. Sounds good? Then let's get started by practicing the

3135
04:12:20,565 --> 04:12:25,612
concepts. In the last exercise, you went through a function's lifecycle. At every

3136
04:12:25,612 --> 04:12:30,722
step, you tested it by calling rowToList on different arguments and checked if the

3137
04:12:30,722 --> 04:12:33,650
return values are correct. This was repetitive.

3138
04:12:33,650 --> 04:12:39,221
tedious and time-consuming. In this lesson, we will learn to write unit tests and

3139
04:12:39,221 --> 04:12:44,998
improve this process. There are many Python libraries for writing unit tests such as

3140
04:12:44,998 --> 04:12:50,706
PyTest, UnitTest, NoseTest, and DocTest. We will use PyTest for this course because

3141
04:12:50,706 --> 04:12:56,002
PyTest has all essential features, is easiest to use, and is the most popular

3142
04:12:56,002 --> 04:12:57,790
testing library in Python.

3143
04:12:57,790 --> 04:13:02,349
To start unit testing with pytest, we will first create a file called

3144
04:13:02,349 --> 04:13:07,636
testRowToList.py. When pytest sees a file name starting with test underscore, it

3145
04:13:07,636 --> 04:13:13,186
understands that this is not an usual Python file, but a special one containing unit

3146
04:13:13,186 --> 04:13:18,671
tests. We must make sure to follow this naming convention. Files holding unit tests

3147
04:13:18,671 --> 04:13:24,222
are also called test modules, and we just created our first test module. In the test

3148
04:13:24,222 --> 04:13:26,270
module, we first import pytest.

3149
04:13:26,270 --> 04:13:31,496
Then we import the function under test. A unit test is written as a Python function

3150
04:13:31,496 --> 04:13:36,408
whose name starts with a test underscore, just like the test module. This way,

3151
04:13:36,408 --> 04:13:41,571
PyTest can tell that it is a unit test and not an ordinary function. The unit test

3152
04:13:41,571 --> 04:13:46,797
usually corresponds to exactly one entry in the argument and return value table for

3153
04:13:46,797 --> 04:13:52,086
rowToList. The unit test checks whether rowToList has the expected return value when

3154
04:13:52,086 --> 04:13:54,290
called on this particular argument.

3155
04:13:54,290 --> 04:13:59,322
This particular argument is a clean row, so we call the unit test test for clean

3156
04:13:59,322 --> 04:14:04,480
row. The actual check is done via an assert statement, and every test must contain

3157
04:14:04,480 --> 04:14:09,575
one. The assert statement has a required first argument, which can be any Boolean

3158
04:14:09,575 --> 04:14:14,544
expression. If the expression is true, the assert statement passes, giving us a

3159
04:14:14,544 --> 04:14:19,010
blank output. If the expression is false, it raises an assertion error.

3160
04:14:19,010 --> 04:14:23,996
In this case, we want to check if rowToList returns the correct list when called on

3161
04:14:23,996 --> 04:14:28,681
the clean row. The expression we use is rowToList called on the argument equal

3162
04:14:28,681 --> 04:14:33,607
equals the correct list. If the function works, this will evaluate to true and the

3163
04:14:33,607 --> 04:14:38,653
assert statement will pass. This will make the test pass. If the function has a bug,

3164
04:14:38,653 --> 04:14:43,519
it will evaluate to false, the assert statement will raise an assertion error and

3165
04:14:43,519 --> 04:14:44,660
the test will fail.

3166
04:14:44,660 --> 04:14:49,666
For the second row in the table, we create a unit test called test on missing area

3167
04:14:49,666 --> 04:14:54,795
because the argument has missing area data. Then we assert that the return value for

3168
04:14:54,795 --> 04:14:59,801
this argument is none. Note that the correct way to check if a variable's value is

3169
04:14:59,801 --> 04:15:04,929
none is to use the boolean expression var is none and not var equal equals none. For

3170
04:15:04,929 --> 04:15:09,631
the third row in the table, we create a unit test called test for missing tab

3171
04:15:09,631 --> 04:15:13,660
because the argument is missing the tab separating area and price.

3172
04:15:13,660 --> 04:15:18,712
The assert statement is similar to the second test. To test whether RotoList is

3173
04:15:18,712 --> 04:15:23,891
