6967
09:03:02,675 --> 09:03:06,940
to put stuff in them. Let's take a look at how objects work.

6968
09:03:06,940 --> 09:03:14,033
The files in S3 buckets are called objects. An object can be anything. An image, a

6969
09:03:14,033 --> 09:03:20,867
video file, CSV, or a log file. Managing objects is a key component of ManyData

6970
09:03:20,867 --> 09:03:27,701
Pipeline. Objects and buckets in S3 work somewhat like files and folders on our

6971
09:03:27,701 --> 09:03:34,622
desktop. Each bucket has a name. Objects names are called keys. A bucket name is

6972
09:03:34,622 --> 09:03:35,660
