09:03:35,660 --> 09:03:42,328
An object's key is the full path of the object from the bucket's root. A bucket's

6974
09:03:42,328 --> 09:03:48,750
name is unique in all of S3. An object's key is unique in the bucket. A bucket

6975
09:03:48,750 --> 09:03:55,665
contains many objects, but an object can only belong to one bucket. First, we create

6976
09:03:55,665 --> 09:04:02,333
the client and assign it to the S3 variable. Now we can perform operations on our

6977
09:04:02,333 --> 09:04:03,980
objects and buckets.

6978
09:04:03,980 --> 09:04:09,087
Let's upload an object into a bucket. We upload the file using the client's

6979
09:04:09,087 --> 09:04:14,739
uploadFile method. The file name is the local file path. Bucket parameter takes the

6980
09:04:14,739 --> 09:04:20,255
name of the bucket we are uploading to. Key is what we want to name the object in

6981
09:04:20,255 --> 09:04:25,566
S3. We are not capturing the return from this method in a variable. The method

