11666
15:18:13,710 --> 15:18:19,450
So, what happens if I try to insert again a new product with the name TrekPowerFly5

11667
15:18:19,450 --> 15:18:24,637
2018? We get this error. We can handle this kind of error using a try-catch

11668
15:18:24,637 --> 15:18:30,377
construct. If you have experience with other programming languages, this syntax may

11669
15:18:30,377 --> 15:18:35,633
look familiar to you. With this try-catch structure, you can implement error

11670
15:18:35,633 --> 15:18:41,028
handling. A try-catch structure is made up of a try-block and a catch-block. A

11671
15:18:41,028 --> 15:18:41,650
try-block

11672
15:18:41,650 --> 15:18:46,683
starts with begin try and ends with end try. A catch block starts with begin catch

11673
15:18:46,683 --> 15:18:51,655
and ends with end catch. You can enclose your statements within the try block. In

11674
15:18:51,655 --> 15:18:56,689
the catch block, you can place your error handling code. If an error occurs in the

11675
15:18:56,689 --> 15:19:01,722
try block, then the catch block takes the control. The catch block is only skipped

11676
15:19:01,722 --> 15:19:06,879
if there is no error in the try block. Let's see some examples. Let's go back to the

11677
15:19:06,879 --> 15:19:08,720
example where we got an error.

11678
15:19:08,720 --> 15:19:13,685
Remember, we tried to insert a new bicycle with a name that was already in the

11679
15:19:13,685 --> 15:19:18,777
product table. Let's enclose this insert statement by a try block. If the insert

11680
15:19:18,777 --> 15:19:23,933
statement is correct, the select statement will display the text product inserted

11681
15:19:23,933 --> 15:19:29,089
correctly. However, if an error occurs, the control will pass to the catch block,

11682
15:19:29,089 --> 15:19:32,590
printing an error occurred, you are in the catch block.

11683
15:19:32,590 --> 15:19:37,890
In this case, as there is an error because we are trying to insert a duplicate name,

11684
15:19:37,890 --> 15:19:43,063
the output will be an error occurred, you are in the catch block. Notice we didn't

11685
15:19:43,063 --> 15:19:48,173
get the same error message as we did without the try-catch construct. Instead, we

11686
15:19:48,173 --> 15:19:53,031
got the message from the SELECT statement. We can also use the print function

11687
15:19:53,031 --> 15:19:58,268
instead of the SELECT statement just for printing the text. For the purpose of this

11688
15:19:58,268 --> 15:20:01,170
course, we will only use the SELECT statement.

11689
15:20:01,170 --> 15:20:06,326
In this example, we are going to see what happens if we insert one product with a

11690
15:20:06,326 --> 15:20:11,673
name which doesn't exist in the database. The insert statement is executed correctly

11691
15:20:11,673 --> 15:20:16,829
and the output is product inserted correctly. We can see that the control doesn't

11692
15:20:16,829 --> 15:20:21,985
pass to the catch block because there are no errors. A try block or a catch block

11693
15:20:21,985 --> 15:20:24,340
can nest another try-catch construct.

11694
15:20:24,340 --> 15:20:29,694
In this example, the catch block has another try-catch construct to handle errors

11695
15:20:29,694 --> 15:20:35,114
encountered by the catch code. Let's imagine that there is an error when trying to

11696
15:20:35,114 --> 15:20:40,203
insert the product. The control passes to the catch block and the insertError

11697
15:20:40,203 --> 15:20:45,755
statement is executed. Then, if another error occurs, the second catch block will be

11698
15:20:45,755 --> 15:20:46,350
executed.

11699
15:20:46,350 --> 15:20:51,704
In this lesson, you will study the anatomy of errors. You will also learn which

11700
15:20:51,704 --> 15:20:57,328
errors can be detected by a TriCAD construct. Do you remember what happened when we

11701
15:20:57,328 --> 15:21:02,817
tried to insert a new product with a name which was already stored in the product

11702
15:21:02,817 --> 15:21:08,374
table? We got this error. The first line of this error has several data which will

11703
15:21:08,374 --> 15:21:13,863
